ions in data engineering. Data Extraction, Transformation, and Loading (ETL) The fundamental steps in data engineering are data extraction, transformation, and loading...</p><p class="reading-time"><i aria-hidden="true" class="fa fa-clock-o"></i> 13 min read <span class="arrow-position"><svg fill="currentColor" height="1.3rem" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="0" viewbox="0 0 512 512" width="1.3rem" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M295.6 163.7c-5.1 5-5.1 13.3-.1 18.4l60.8 60.9H124.9c-7.1 0-12.9 5.8-12.9 13s5.8 13 12.9 13h231.3l-60.8 60.9c-5 5.1-4.9 13.3.1 18.4 5.1 5 13.2 5 18.3-.1l82.4-83c1.1-1.2 2-2.5 2.7-4.1.7-1.6 1-3.3 1-5 0-3.4-1.3-6.6-3.7-9.1l-82.4-83c-4.9-5.2-13.1-5.3-18.2-.3z"></path></svg></span></p></a></li><li><a class="related-post-item" href="data-science-deciphered-what-is-a-spline"><h3 class="h3">Data Science Deciphered: What is a Spline?</h3><p class="related-post-content">In the ever-evolving world of data science, strategies to analyze, interpret, and visualize statistics play a crucial position. One such technique is the usage of splines-a concept rooted in arithmetic however widely applied throughout numerous fields. But what exactly is a spline, and why is...</p><p class="reading-time"><i aria-hidden="true" class="fa fa-clock-o"></i> 7 min read <span class="arrow-position"><svg fill="currentColor" height="1.3rem" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="0" viewbox="0 0 512 512" width="1.3rem" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M295.6 163.7c-5.1 5-5.1 13.3-.1 18.4l60.8 60.9H124.9c-7.1 0-12.9 5.8-12.9 13s5.8 13 12.9 13h231.3l-60.8 60.9c-5 5.1-4.9 13.3.1 18.4 5.1 5 13.2 5 18.3-.1l82.4-83c1.1-1.2 2-2.5 2.7-4.1.7-1.6 1-3.3 1-5 0-3.4-1.3-6.6-3.7-9.1l-82.4-83c-4.9-5.2-13.1-5.3-18.2-.3z"></path></svg></span></p></a></li><li><a class="related-post-item" href="five-ways-to-detect-outliers-anomalies-that-every-data-scientist-should-know-python-code"><h3 class="h3">Five Ways to Detect Outliers/Anomalies That Every Data Scientist Should Know